# Windows batch files are CRLF. A ZIP download or a Linux checkout would otherwise
# give run.bat bare LF. cmd.exe's goto is reported to miss labels in such files; an
# LF copy did not show that on Windows 10 (2026-11-02), so this is a precaution.
run.bat text eol=crlf

# progettoSnaps-format test INIs are CRLF, as the real files are. Keep the bytes as
# written so the parser tests read CRLF on every platform.
tests/parser/fixtures/*.ini -text
